# Distribution boundary for reyemtech/laravel-hubspot.
#
# `export-ignore` controls what `git archive` emits, which is what Packagist serves as this
# package's dist tarball and therefore what lands in a consumer's `vendor/` directory. Without
# this file every path in the repository shipped -- the planning corpus, the whole Astro docs
# site, the test suite and every tool config. That is bandwidth a consumer pays for and cannot
# use.
#
# What stays in the tarball is the runtime surface plus the files a consumer or an auditor may
# legitimately need offline: `src/`, `config/`, `database/`, `resources/`, `composer.json`,
# `README.md`, `LICENSE`, `SECURITY.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`.
#
# What is excluded is development-only. Excluding `tests/` is the one line worth stating a reason
# for: consumers cannot run this package's suite anyway -- it needs `orchestra/testbench` and the
# dev requires, none of which are installed transitively -- so shipping it only adds weight. The
# suite remains available to anyone who clones the repository, which is where it is run.
#
# `export-ignore` affects `git archive` only. A clone is unaffected, so CI, which clones, sees
# every path as before.

/.claude            export-ignore
/.github            export-ignore
/.planning          export-ignore
/docs               export-ignore
/scripts            export-ignore
/site               export-ignore
/tests              export-ignore

/BRIEF.md           export-ignore
/CLAUDE.md          export-ignore
/STANDARDS.md       export-ignore

/.gitattributes     export-ignore
/.gitignore         export-ignore
/.npmrc             export-ignore
/commitlint.config.mjs      export-ignore
/phpcs.xml          export-ignore
/phpstan.neon       export-ignore
/phpunit.xml.dist   export-ignore
/pint.json          export-ignore
/pnpm-lock.yaml     export-ignore
/pnpm-workspace.yaml        export-ignore
/release-please-config.json export-ignore
/.release-please-manifest.json      export-ignore
